nerdcommenter
=============

[count] is optional. Most commands also work on a visual selection.

CUSTOM
  =                         Toggle comments (normal and visual mode). Mapped to
                            <leader>c<space> in the vimrc

COMMENT
  [count]<leader>cc         Comment out the line or the selection
  [count]<leader>cn         Same as <leader>cc, but force nesting
  [count]<leader>cm         Comment with one set of multipart delimiters
  [count]<leader>cs         "Sexy" comment: a block layout
  [count]<leader>cy         Same as <leader>cc, but yank the lines first
  [count]<leader>cl / [count]<leader>cb
                            Same as <leader>cc, with delimiters aligned on the left / both
                            sides
  <leader>c$                Comment from the cursor to the end of the line
  <leader>cA                Add delimiters at the end of the line and insert between them

TOGGLE AND UNCOMMENT
  [count]<leader>c<space>   Toggle. If the top line is commented, uncomment all lines, and
                            the reverse
  [count]<leader>ci         Toggle each line on its own
  [count]<leader>cu         Uncomment

DELIMITERS
  <leader>ca                Switch to the alternative delimiters
